			"Message": "build(deps): bump @xterm/xterm from 6.1.0-beta.203 to 6.1.0-beta.204\n\nBumps [@xterm/xterm](https://github.com/xtermjs/xterm.js) from 6.1.0-beta.203 to 6.1.0-beta.204.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/xtermjs/xterm.js/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/xtermjs/xterm.js/commits)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: \"@xterm/xterm\"\n  dependency-version: 6.1.0-beta.204\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>",
			"SHA": "6da9229fbf6ea116a33f6277f731369cd3b5a33d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-28T00:02:49Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠁⠀⠀⠀",
				103,
				23
			],
			"Message": "feat: Implement bundled workbench structure for Browser, Electron, Sessions, and base Workbench\n\n- Introduced new entry and layout files for bundled Browser, Electron, Sessions, and base Workbench.\n- Refactored existing Bootstrap and ServicesProxy files to streamline error handling.\n- Enhanced performance measurement for various components during the bootstrapping process.\n- Updated astro.config.ts to support bundled workbench inputs and outputs, ensuring compatibility with existing build profiles.\n- Improved error handling and logging throughout the Electron and WindPreload modules.\n- Added new routes for bundled Browser, Electron, Sessions, and Workbench in the Astro pages.\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>",
			"SHA": "be93a3d3b4cf158b50a2f53ebfbd590c7dfbd3ca"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T21:26:49Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				85,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Add persistent PostHog device identifier\n\nAdd GetOrCreateSkyIdentifier() function to generate and persist a stable device identifier in localStorage. The previous implementation used Date.now() which created a new random identifier on every page load, preventing consistent user/device tracking across sessions.\n\nThe new identifier follows the format `land-dev-sky-{8-char-random}` and is stored under the key `land-posthog-id`. On subsequent loads, the existing identifier is retrieved from localStorage, enabling PostHog to properly track unique users and maintain device-level analytics continuity.\n\nThis integrates with the existing PostHog bootstrap configuration in PostHogBridge.ts.",
			"SHA": "5b3e6c0fcf74f3912ad7efe330c96d19f862e6c9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T21:11:34Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				85,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Add webview-view update and event forwarding handlers\n\nAdd two new SkyBridge capabilities for complete webview-view integration:\n\n1. `sky://webview/updateView` handler - Bridges Cocoon `view.title` / `view.description` / `view.badge` setter notifications to update the parked workbench `WebviewView`. Dispatches `cel:webview:updateView` for observers.\n\n2. Workbench → Extension event forwarding - Inside the view registration block, subscribe to workbench events and forward them to Cocoon:\n   - `WebviewView.webview.onDidReceivedMessage` → `webview.message` notification\n   - `WebviewView.onDidChangeVisibility` → `webview.viewState` notification\n   - `WebviewView.onDispose` → `webview.dispose` notification AND cleanup of `__CEL_WEBVIEW_VIEWS__` registry\n\nThis completes the webview-view lifecycle: register → resolve → set-html → update-metadata → communicate → dispose.",
			"SHA": "c708338bda9738970b433105895f09edff3498f1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T21:02:41Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				85,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Add webview-view set-html and postMessage handlers\n\nAdd two new SkyBridge handlers to complete the webview-view integration path:\n\n1. `sky://webview/set-html` - When a Cocoon-side `resolveWebviewView` callback sets `view.webview.html`, Mountain re-emits the `webview.setHtml` notification. This handler looks up the parked workbench `WebviewView` (registered via prior `sky://webview/registerView`) by viewId from `__CEL_WEBVIEW_VIEWS__` and applies the HTML to its real `webview.html` setter so the panel paints. Also dispatches `cel:webview:set-html` DOM event for Sky-side observers.\n\n2. `sky://webview/postMessage` - When an extension calls `view.webview.postMessage(msg)`, the notification is forwarded to this handler. It dispatches `cel:webview:post-message` and forwards the message to the parked workbench view's webview when a viewId match exists.\n\nBoth handlers integrate with the parked `__CEL_WEBVIEW_VIEWS__` registry created during view registration, completing the full lifecycle: register → resolve (set-html) → communicate (postMessage) → unregister.",
			"SHA": "40ca326cd1e83be0b745fa0ba5fe8c9d62dd0a69"
		}
	],
